---
description: Marketing Next.js, SEO, localization, attribution, and validation rules
globs:
  - "src/**/*.ts"
  - "src/**/*.tsx"
  - "scripts/**/*.mjs"
  - "tests/**/*.ts"
  - "docs/seo/**/*.md"
  - "package.json"
alwaysApply: false
---

- `docs/seo/SEO_SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md` is canonical; `docs/SEO_SOURCE_OF_TRUTH.md` is only a compatibility pointer.
- Preserve self-canonicals, eligible reciprocal hreflang, sitemap policy, UTM/gclid/srsltid handoff, and allowlisted non-PII analytics events.
- Do not bulk-index untranslated/partial locales, force IP language redirects, or infer geography from language.
- Merchant Center pages describe configured products but never modify Stripe prices, checkout, tax, or subscription logic.
- Search Console tooling is read-only. Credential files and routine output remain outside Git.
- Use npm and preserve `package-lock.json`; run focused SEO tests, lint, locale parity/ASCII checks, build, and runtime/canonical audits as applicable.
